    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45422.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Well, I've been in this week. I've been in Murray, Paducah. I'm on my way to Henderson now, so I'm in the far western part of my district. But, you know, I have 35 counties. Of course, I live in Thompsonville, but we just try to cover as many counties as possible on days when I'm not in Washington and The town halls are a great way to invite people in the talk to the congressman. If they have questions or concerns, I'd do it in a public setting and very transparent way and try to answer the questions or listen to their concerns. But when you have 35 counties, it's great to see the rural atmosphere of Kentucky and listen to everyone's opinions. It seems like Everybody has a different opinion,",
