    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45422.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "It's huge. In fact, we've already attracted hundreds of millions of dollars of private sector investment. And this wasn't something that the state of Kentucky had to come in and give them tax incentives and free money and all this. This is the private sector, a product that's in high demand and that's hemp. So we just, because we took bold steps in 2013 to become the first state in the United States to legally grow hemp, we're reaping the benefits now. And too often, Kentucky is not the first and closer to the last and trying to do something innovative. We took a chance here I'm very proud of the work that we did at the Department of Agriculture when I was Commissioner of Agriculture since then, Senator McConnell has come on board and really helped us on the federal level. So I think we've got a really good industry here in rural Kentucky and that's the hemp industry.",
