    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 45422,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45422.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 50,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's vital that we have the US MCA for agriculture and it's vital for the American workers. What the US MCA is, is essentially the new NAFTA. And this is the new NAFTA that President Trump negotiated. So it's a better deal for workers, and it's a better deal for rural America. And this new NAFTA, it also addresses some concerns we add with stealing patents, and currency manipulation, and intellectual property. I think that the deal that the President made with the new NAFTA, which is the USMCA, US-Mexico-Canada Agreement, will be very beneficial to South Central Kentucky. It's very beneficial to agriculture in the automotive parts industry, which are two big employers in our area. A lot of the things that we produce in South Central Kentucky, the raw materials come from Canada and Mexico. So this just ensures that we will continue to have good trade relations with Mexico and Canada, but it doesn't create a situation where Mexico or Canada have an unfair advantage to the United States, which they did before. And certainly China does. But the president's still negotiating that deal with China. It's a bilateral deal between the United States and China. And I hope that he's successful in that. But in the meantime, we need to pass the notify the president's USMCA. And I'm working very closely with President Trump to try to get the votes in Congress to make that happen.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
